## Why This Is Asked

Gauges ability to justify product bets with a pragmatic, numbers-driven approach and to handle uncertainty in inputs.

## Key Concepts

- Cost estimation
- Benefit estimation
- Break-even analysis
- Reasonable assumptions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple CBA calculator
function cba(params) {
  const {maU, lift, arpu, months, cost} = params;
  const annualizedBenefit = maU * lift * arpu * months;
  return {annualizedBenefit, cost, breakevenMonths: cost / (annualizedBenefit || 1)};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust if MAU grows or adoption changes?
- What if ARPU uplift is not uniform across user segments?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess understanding of privacy-preserving, on-device analytics and the viability of data-sharing via aggregates.

## Key Concepts

- On-device analytics and data minimization
- User consent and opt-in UX
- Aggregated data leakage risk and privacy controls
- Cost modeling: device runtime, memory, and backend bandwidth
- Rollout strategy, drift monitoring, and governance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple rolling aggregate for 90-day window on-device
function rollingAvg(values, window=90) {
  let sum=0;
  const res=[];
  for(let i=0;i<values.length;i++){
    sum+=values[i];
    if(i>=window) sum-=values[i-window];
    if(i>=window-1) res.push(sum/(window));
  }
  return res;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate accuracy of aggregates vs server baselines?
- What are rollback or revocation strategies if consent changes mid-rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical on-device crypto trade-offs for privacy-focused apps.

## Key Concepts
- On-device key management
- Key rotation cadence
- AES-256-GCM encryption
- Impact on battery, CPU, memory
- Privacy/compliance costs

## Code Example
```javascript
async function encryptNote(note, key) {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const alg = { name: 'AES-GCM', iv };
  const ciphertext = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(alg, key, enc.encode(note));
  return { iv, ciphertext: new Uint8Array(ciphertext) };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to measure encryption energy impact on mobile?
- How to rotate keys without re-encrypting all notes?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a lightweight edge optimization with clear cost/benefit trade-offs, focusing on data movement, energy, and privacy in mobile environments.

## Key Concepts

- Content-based fingerprinting
- Bloom filters for on-device dedup
- Bandwidth vs CPU energy trade-offs
- Privacy considerations and optional cloud verification

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: compute hash and check Bloom filter
function canSend(record, bloom) {
  const h = hash(record); // deterministic fingerprint
  if (bloom.mightContain(h)) return false;
  bloom.add(h);
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you estimate Bloom filter false positive rate given device memory constraints?
- How would you rollout to mitigate drift in data patterns and ensure continued value?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses designing a privacy-conscious, on-device NLP feature with energy, storage, and regulatory constraints, plus a quantified cost-benefit trade-off.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML and multilingual support
- Energy budgeting, latency targets, local storage planning
- Privacy budgets, regulatory/compliance costs, opt-in controls
- Staged rollout and metrics for go/no-go decisions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo inference loop for on-device summarization
function summarize(conversation, model) {
  // assume preloaded model in memory
  const chunk = chunkify(conversation, 512);
  return chunk.map(c => model.infer(c)).join(" ");
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate privacy guarantees during updates?
- How would you measure missed insights vs. privacy budget over time?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design cost-aware, privacy-preserving on-device learning with federation. Evaluate cross-app data leverage, regulatory implications, and rollout strategy across regions.

## Key Concepts

- Federated learning and secure aggregation
- On-device resource budgeting (CPU, memory, energy)
- Model drift telemetry and anomaly tracking
- Regulatory/compliance costs and rollout governance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: federated update cycle outline
while (serviceRunning) {
  const localBatch = collectLocalSignals();
  const grads = computeGradients(localBatch);
  const encGrads = secureAggregate(grads);
  sendToServer(encGrads);
  updateLocalModelIfNeeded();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure drift and trigger model refresh?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate ROI without exposing data?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate edge ML costs into a robust business case, including privacy constraints, rollout risk, and financial metrics.

## Key Concepts
- On-device RL inference energy and latency
- Policy delta encoding and secure transmission
- Drift/maintenance costs and OTA rollout
- Privacy/compliance and data minimization
- Rollout strategy and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-cost estimator
function estimateCost(params) {
  const {
    dispatchesPerHour, energyPerDispatch, latencyMs,
    cloudSavingsPerDispatch
  } = params;
  // simplified calculation
  return energyPerDispatch * dispatchesPerHour / 3600;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate model drift in production and trigger rollback?
- What would you put in the go/no-go criteria to scale beyond pilot?
